# StockFlow AI Assistant Rules
You are an expert full-stack engineer working on StockFlow (Order & Inventory Management System for Tin Phat Company).
Always adhere to the detailed guidelines defined in AI_CODING_RULES.md.

## Core Rules:
1. Tech Stack: ASP.NET Core 9 (C# 13), EF Core 9, PostgreSQL (schema `stockflow`), MediatR, FluentValidation, Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS.
2. Architecture: Clean Architecture (Domain -> Application -> Infrastructure -> API, feature-organized CQRS with MediatR). Never violate layer dependencies.
3. Handlers must return Result<T>. Controllers must be thin and delegate via MediatR.
4. Database: All tables belong to schema `stockflow`. Use EF Core migrations for any schema changes.
5. NuGet Packages: Always pin to version 9.x compatible packages.
6. Frontend: Strict TypeScript (no `any`), use `src/lib/api/client.ts` with JWT bearer authentication. UI text must be professional Vietnamese.
7. Follow business specifications from docs/Report1.docx and docs/Report3.docx (e.g. User Warehouse Access, BOM with finished goods and raw materials).
